From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:45:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Limit the extra swapchain image workaround to DOOM.

The imported wineland-child-rendering/0083 patch by Erhan Bilgili requests
an extra swapchain image when the application asks for the host surface
minimum. It addresses DOOM Eternal and DOOM: The Dark Ages but currently
changes the request for every application, on both X11 and Wayland.

Hades' native Vulkan renderer uses three-entry per-image resource arrays.
Its shipped PDB identifies the startup crash as
sgg::ForgeRenderer::CmdRecord_BeginFrame, forgerenderer.cpp:4317, while
dereferencing pCmdPool[gFrameIndex] before vkResetCommandPool. A fourth
image index reaches the adjacent gScreenshotMutex instead; its -1 debug
information marker matches the invalid pointer in the crash log.

Restrict the extra-image adjustment to the two intended game executables.
Match the basename case-insensitively rather than depending on Steam IDs,
so non-Steam installations retain the same workaround. Keep the original
minimum/maximum and overflow checks. Do not cap or remap host image indices.

The original import and its upstream attribution remain unchanged. This
follow-up must be applied after wineland-child-rendering/0083.
---
 dlls/win32u/vulkan.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -4288,6 +4288,20 @@
     return VK_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+static BOOL needs_extra_swapchain_image(void)
+{
+    static const WCHAR doom_eternalW[] =
+        {'D','O','O','M','E','t','e','r','n','a','l','x','6','4','v','k','.','e','x','e',0};
+    static const WCHAR doom_dark_agesW[] =
+        {'D','O','O','M','T','h','e','D','a','r','k','A','g','e','s','.','e','x','e',0};
+    const WCHAR *p, *name = NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ProcessParameters->ImagePathName.Buffer;
+
+    if (!name) return FALSE;
+    if ((p = wcsrchr( name, '/' ))) name = p + 1;
+    if ((p = wcsrchr( name, '\\' ))) name = p + 1;
+    return !wcsicmp( name, doom_eternalW ) || !wcsicmp( name, doom_dark_agesW );
+}
+
 static VkResult win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR( VkDevice client_device, const VkSwapchainCreateInfoKHR *create_info,
                                              const VkAllocationCallbacks *allocator, VkSwapchainKHR *ret )
 {
@@ -4328,10 +4342,9 @@ static VkResult win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR( VkDevice client_device, const VkSwapcha
     create_info_host.imageExtent.width = max( create_info_host.imageExtent.width, capabilities.minImageExtent.width );
     create_info_host.imageExtent.height = max( create_info_host.imageExtent.height, capabilities.minImageExtent.height );
 
-    /* DOOM Eternal and DOOM: The Dark Ages rely on an extra image to continue
-     * acquiring while an earlier image is still pending presentation. Request
-     * one when the application asks for exactly the surface minimum. */
-    if (capabilities.minImageCount < UINT32_MAX &&
+    /* Restrict the extra-image workaround to the DOOM games. Hades, for
+     * example, has fixed-size per-image resource arrays. */
+    if (needs_extra_swapchain_image() && capabilities.minImageCount < UINT32_MAX &&
         create_info_host.minImageCount == capabilities.minImageCount &&
         (!capabilities.maxImageCount || capabilities.minImageCount < capabilities.maxImageCount))
     {
